WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:07.839 align:start position:19%
In 1897, a dead woman walked into an
American courtroom and pointed at her

00:00:05.359 --> 00:00:12.800 align:start position:19%
killer. The jury heard her testimony.
They believed her and they sent a man to

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:18.320 align:start position:19%
prison for life based on the word of a
ghost. This is the only murder trial in

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:22.880 align:start position:19%
American history where a ghost took the
stand. And the strangest part, the

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:28.000 align:start position:19%
evidence says she might have been
telling the truth. Welcome back to

00:00:25.039 --> 00:00:35.040 align:start position:19%
Unsolved Shadows, where the past refuses
to stay buried. Today, the Greenbryer

00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:40.879 align:start position:19%
ghost, a rushed burial, a grieving
mother, and four midnight visits that

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:46.480 align:start position:19%
changed everything. Quick question
before we start. If a ghost told you who

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:54.320 align:start position:19%
the killer was, would you believe it?
Hold that fort. Greenbryer County, West

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:59.840 align:start position:19%
Virginia. January 23rd, 1897.
A cold Saturday afternoon. A neighbor

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:06.640 align:start position:19%
boy runs an errand to the little house
of Edward Shu and his young wife Zona.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:12.000 align:start position:19%
What he finds inside stops him cold.
Zona Heast Shu is dead. 23 years old.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:17.360 align:start position:19%
Her husband Edward, they called him
Trout, is kneeling beside her, cradling

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:22.080 align:start position:19%
her head in his arms, rocking back and
forth, sobbing. Now, here is the first

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:27.759 align:start position:19%
strange thing. When neighbors try to
help to move her to look closer, Trout

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:32.560 align:start position:19%
will not let go. He clutches her head
like he is hiding something. Dr. George

00:01:30.479 --> 00:01:36.799 align:start position:19%
Knap arrives. He tries to examine the
body properly, but Trout hovers over him

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:41.439 align:start position:19%
the entire time, rushing him,
distracting him, answering questions

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:45.920 align:start position:19%
nobody asked. The examination lasts
barely 30 minutes. The doctor writes

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:51.360 align:start position:19%
down the cause of death. Quote,
"Everlasting faint."

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:55.920 align:start position:19%
Everlasting faint. That is not a medical
diagnosis. That is a shrug with a

00:01:53.520 --> 00:02:01.119 align:start position:19%
signature. A few days later, the doctor
quietly changes it to child bed fever.

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:06.719 align:start position:19%
Zona might have been expecting a child.
Nobody really knows. But a proper

00:02:03.119 --> 00:02:11.599 align:start position:19%
autopsy never happens. Not yet. And
Trout, he moves fast. Zona is buried the

00:02:09.679 --> 00:02:16.319 align:start position:19%
very next day before rumors can grow
legs, before questions can be asked. But

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:21.440 align:start position:19%
people notice things. At the burial,
Zona wears a dress with a stiff, high

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:26.160 align:start position:19%
collar, buttoned all the way up, hiding
her neck completely, and Trout places a

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:32.560 align:start position:19%
rolledup cloth beside her head in the
coffin, like a pillow, like support for

00:02:30.239 --> 00:02:37.840 align:start position:19%
a neck that might need holding together.
Now, let me tell you about Trout Shoe

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:42.879 align:start position:19%
because this man, this man has a past.
He drifted into Greenbryer County from

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:50.319 align:start position:19%
out of state. charming, good-looking,
and married twice before Zona. His first

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:56.480 align:start position:19%
wife died under unclear circumstances.
His second wife divorced him, claiming

00:02:53.040 --> 00:03:01.280 align:start position:19%
cruelty. He served time for horse theft.
This is not a man with clean hands.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:06.480 align:start position:19%
Zona's mother, Mary Jane Hasta, never
trusted him. And at that rushed funeral,

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:10.080 align:start position:19%
watching that high collar, a mother's
instinct starts screaming. Mary Jane

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:14.879 align:start position:19%
goes home and does something
extraordinary. Every night for four

00:03:12.159 --> 00:03:20.239 align:start position:19%
weeks, she prays. Not for comfort, for
the truth. Show me what happened to my

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:25.440 align:start position:19%
daughter. And then on the fourth week,
Zona comes home. Not once. Four nights

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:30.159 align:start position:19%
in a row. The ghost of Zoner appears to
her mother glowing faintly, and tells

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:34.879 align:start position:19%
her everything. She says Trout came home
angry. Supper was not ready. He flew

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:39.440 align:start position:19%
into a rage and broke her neck with his
bare hands. And then the ghost does

00:03:36.959 --> 00:03:45.920 align:start position:19%
something Mary Jane will never forget.
Slowly, she turns her head all the way

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:51.360 align:start position:19%
around. A full half turn no living neck
could survive to prove it was murder to

00:03:48.799 --> 00:03:57.200 align:start position:19%
show her mother exactly how she died. A
broken neck displayed like evidence. Now

00:03:54.799 --> 00:04:02.640 align:start position:19%
stop. Take a breath because I know what
you are thinking. Grief does strange

00:03:59.519 --> 00:04:07.040 align:start position:19%
things to people. Dreams feel real. Was
this just a heartbroken mother imagining

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:12.159 align:start position:19%
what she needed to hear? That is the
reasonable question and it is exactly

00:04:09.439 --> 00:04:17.919 align:start position:19%
what the town thought until Mary Jane
did something nobody expected. She went

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:24.479 align:start position:19%
to the prosecutor. Prosecutor John
Alfred Preston listens to this wild

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:29.680 align:start position:19%
story. A ghost. Four visits. A broken
neck. He should laugh her out of the

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:37.280 align:start position:19%
office. Instead, he orders the body
exumed. Think about that. In 1897,

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:43.520 align:start position:19%
a prosecutor digs up a woman because her
mother dreamed her ghost said so. Either

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:49.680 align:start position:19%
he saw something in Mary Jane's eyes or
he already suspected trout, too. The

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:56.240 align:start position:19%
autopsy happens in a small schoolhouse.
Three doctors and what they find freezes

00:04:53.440 --> 00:05:01.759 align:start position:19%
the room. Zona's neck was broken between
the first and second vertebrae. Her

00:04:58.639 --> 00:05:06.560 align:start position:19%
windpipe crushed. her throat bruised
with what looked like finger marks.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:09.440 align:start position:19%
Exactly what the ghost is down the
mystery shadow.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:14.160 align:start position:19%
&gt;&gt; A mother who never saw the body up
close, knew precisely how her daughter

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:19.840 align:start position:19%
died. Now, how could Mary Jane know
that? She was not at the autopsy. She

00:05:17.199 --> 00:05:25.840 align:start position:19%
never examined the body. Trout guarded
it like a secret unless someone told

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:31.039 align:start position:19%
her. Trout Shu is arrested for murder
and in June of 1897, he stands trial in

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:35.039 align:start position:19%
Greenbryer County. The courtroom is
packed. Reporters come from three states

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:41.039 align:start position:19%
because everyone has heard the rumor.
The ghost is going to testify. Mary Jane

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:45.680 align:start position:19%
Hista takes the stand. And under oath,
she tells the jury about the four

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:50.479 align:start position:19%
visits. The glowing figure, the head
turning all the way around, the

00:05:47.759 --> 00:05:56.639 align:start position:19%
accusation from beyond the grave. If you
enjoy mysteries like this one, subscribe

00:05:53.440 --> 00:06:01.680 align:start position:19%
to Unsolved Shadows right now because
next week we have a case that is somehow

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:08.880 align:start position:19%
even stranger than a testifying ghost.
Here is the wild part. The judge allows

00:06:04.479 --> 00:06:14.560 align:start position:19%
it. The defense barely objects. In 1897
West Virginia, ghost testimony enters

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:19.039 align:start position:19%
the official court record. The defense
tries to paint Mary Jane as a grieving

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:24.319 align:start position:19%
woman lost in fantasy, but she never
waivers. Four weeks of prayer, four

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:30.319 align:start position:19%
midnight visits, every detail, steady as
stone. Then the prosecution plays its

00:06:26.479 --> 00:06:34.720 align:start position:19%
real card. Not the ghost, the body, the
broken neck, the broken neck, the

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:40.160 align:start position:19%
cushioned wong, the cresened wong, the
cresen, the crushed windpipe, the

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:46.400 align:start position:19%
finger-shaped bruises. Science backing
up the supernatural and trout on the

00:06:43.039 --> 00:06:51.280 align:start position:19%
stand. He is cold, charming at first,
then cracking. His story about that

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:56.240 align:start position:19%
afternoon keeps shifting. Small lies,
then bigger ones. Witnesses remember the

00:06:53.680 --> 00:07:01.680 align:start position:19%
high collar at the funeral, the rolled
cloth in the coffin, the way he would

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:07.120 align:start position:19%
not let go of her head. Every strange
detail suddenly looks like guilt. The

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:12.720 align:start position:19%
jury deliberates for just over an hour,
one hour for a murder trial built partly

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:17.680 align:start position:19%
on a ghost story. Guilty. First-degree
murder. Edward Troutshu is sentenced to

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:23.759 align:start position:19%
life in prison. He maintains his
innocence to the end. Three years later

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:30.880 align:start position:19%
in 1900, Troutu dies in prison during an
epidemic. He takes whatever he knows to

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:36.720 align:start position:19%
his own grave. So, was justice served by
a ghost? Or did a clever, grieving

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:41.840 align:start position:19%
mother simply know her son-in-law was a
killer and invent the only witness no

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:47.199 align:start position:19%
lawyer could cross-examine? Let us look
at this like investigators. Theory one,

00:07:44.479 --> 00:07:52.400 align:start position:19%
the supernatural is real and Zona truly
came back. The broken neck detail is

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:58.479 align:start position:19%
hard to explain any other way. Theory
two. Mary Jane already suspected murder.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:04.319 align:start position:19%
Mothers noticed things. The rushed
burial, the collar. Trout's past. Her

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:08.960 align:start position:19%
subconscious assembled the puzzle and
her dreams delivered the verdict. Theory

00:08:06.879 --> 00:08:14.560 align:start position:19%
three, the cynical one. She made the
whole thing up. A brilliant lie. Because

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:20.400 align:start position:19%
in 1897, no court would dig up a body on
a mother's hunch. But a ghost that got

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:24.800 align:start position:19%
the prosecutor's attention. And here is
what really gets me about this case.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:30.560 align:start position:19%
Whatever you believe about ghosts, the
physical evidence was real. A broken

00:08:27.199 --> 00:08:36.399 align:start position:19%
neck does not lie. Someone murdered Zona
Heista Shu. My personal theory. I think

00:08:33.519 --> 00:08:40.240 align:start position:19%
Mary Jane knew. Maybe not consciously,
not at first, but she watched Trout at

00:08:38.479 --> 00:08:44.720 align:start position:19%
that funeral, clutching and hovering,
and some deep maternal instinct did the

00:08:42.479 --> 00:08:49.760 align:start position:19%
math before her mind caught up. the
dreams, the ghosts, the four visits. I

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:54.160 align:start position:19%
think that was her grief and her
certainty finding the only language

00:08:52.000 --> 00:09:00.240 align:start position:19%
powerful enough to force the world to
listen. And you know what? It worked.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:06.240 align:start position:19%
But I will say this, if it was all
invention, how did she describe the

00:09:02.959 --> 00:09:10.800 align:start position:19%
exact broken vertebrae? That detail
still gives me chills more than a

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:15.360 align:start position:19%
century later. The Greenbryer ghost
remains the only case in American legal

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:20.880 align:start position:19%
history where testimony from beyond the
grave helped convict a killer. No court

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:27.120 align:start position:19%
has allowed it since. Today, a
historical marker stands in Greenbryer

00:09:22.959 --> 00:09:32.160 align:start position:19%
County. It reads, quote, "Only known
case in which testimony from a ghost

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:37.839 align:start position:19%
helped convict a murderer. Locals still
whisper that on cold January nights, a

00:09:35.519 --> 00:09:44.800 align:start position:19%
woman in white walks the road near the
old shoe house, waiting,

00:09:41.519 --> 00:09:51.360 align:start position:19%
watching, making sure the truth stays
buried or stays told. So, what do you

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:56.800 align:start position:19%
think happened that night in Greenbryer
County? A genuine haunting, a mother's

00:09:54.560 --> 00:10:01.040 align:start position:19%
brilliant deception, or something in
between that we do not have a name for

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:05.279 align:start position:19%
yet? Drop your theory in the comments. I
read every single one and the best ones

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:08.560 align:start position:19%
might just shape our next investigation.
And if this case kept you up tonight,

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:12.800 align:start position:19%
wait until you hear about the lighthouse
keepers who vanished without a trace,

00:10:10.399 --> 00:10:18.399 align:start position:19%
leaving dinner still warm on the table.
That story is coming soon. If you are

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:23.440 align:start position:19%
new here, subscribe to Unsolved Shadows.
We dig up history's darkest mysteries.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:23.440 align:start position:19%
So you do.

